    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>This is what a weeknight looks like at Kayla Dunham&rsquo;s house: one protein, a pile of vegetables, and nothing that takes longer than the air fryer takes to preheat. Seatopia King Salmon gets sea salt, cracked black pepper, and red chili flakes, then a generous drizzle of hot honey and a lemon slice on top. Eight to ten minutes at 400&deg;F and the honey caramelizes into a lacquered, faintly spicy crust.</p><p>Underneath it: a bed of spinach, air-fried Japanese sweet potato rounds, and a cucumber-and-tomato salad dressed with nothing but olive oil, lemon, salt, and pepper. Total time is about 25 minutes, and most of that is the sweet potato cooking while you slice everything else.</p><p>We built it around Seatopia <a href=\"/products/king-salmon\" title=\"Seatopia King Salmon\">King Salmon</a> from <a href=\"/pages/ora-king-salmon-new-zealand\" title=\"Ora King, New Zealand\">Ora King</a> in New Zealand &mdash; 8.5 oz skin-on, sushi-grade portions, lab tested to the <a href=\"/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters\" title=\"Why Clean Seafood Matters\">Seatopia Standard&trade;</a> for mercury, microplastics, and nutrient density. It is a rich, high-fat fillet, which is exactly what you want under honey and heat.</p><p>Kayla is a creator and community builder in Los Angeles who works in partnerships at Spotify and organizes with <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/westsidecoastalclub/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Westside Coastal Club on Instagram\">Westside Coastal Club</a>. The whole ethos is <em>leave it better than you found it</em> &mdash; which is a pretty good description of how we think about sourcing fish, too.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_intro"
      ],
