            "heading": "About 25 minutes",
            "text": "<p>Roughly 15 minutes of prep and 10 minutes of cooking. Start the sweet potato first and everything else &mdash; salmon, salad, greens &mdash; happens while it roasts.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "glance_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 2",
            "text": "<p>Two King Salmon portions, one medium Japanese sweet potato, one Persian cucumber, a cup of cherry tomatoes. Scale it straight up for four; nothing needs recalculating.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "glance_heat": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "lightning",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "400&deg;F for 8&ndash;10 minutes",
            "text": "<p>Air fryer, no flipping, no pan to scrub. The honey does the work &mdash; it caramelizes at the edges while the inside stays translucent and soft.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "glance_pantry": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Five things on the fish",
            "text": "<p>Hot honey, red chili flakes, sea salt, cracked black pepper, lemon. There is no marinade, no sauce to whisk, and nothing to thicken.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
