    "on_the_plate": {
      "type": "multicolumn-with-icons",
      "blocks": {
        "part_greens": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "box",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "1. A bed of greens",
            "text": "<p>Two cups of baby spinach, raw and undressed. The hot salmon wilts it just enough on contact, and the warm honey drips down and dresses it for you.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "part_salmon": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "lightning",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "2. Hot honey King Salmon",
            "text": "<p>Patted dry, seasoned hard with salt, pepper, and chili flakes, drizzled with hot honey and topped with a lemon slice. Air fried until the top lacquers and the edges char.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "part_potato": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "organic",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "3. Air fryer sweet potato",
            "text": "<p>A Japanese sweet potato in thick rounds, tossed with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Purple skin, pale gold inside, drier and sweeter than an orange sweet potato.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "part_salad": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "star",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "4. Cucumber and tomato",
            "text": "<p>Sliced Persian cucumber and halved cherry tomatoes with olive oil, salt, and pepper. This is the acid and the crunch, and it is what keeps the honey from taking over.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
