    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "step_potato": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/kayla-dunham-air-fryer-japanese-sweet-potato-rounds.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 0",
            "heading": "Sweet potato goes in first",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Slice one medium Japanese sweet potato into thick rounds &mdash; about &frac12; inch, so they stay creamy in the middle. Toss with olive oil, sea salt, and black pepper, then roast or air fry until tender and golden at the edges, roughly 15 minutes at 400&deg;F. It is the longest-cooking thing on the plate, so it starts alone.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_salmon": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/kayla-dunham-king-salmon-hot-honey-seasoned.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 5",
            "heading": "Season the King Salmon",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Pat both portions completely dry &mdash; this is the one step people skip and the one that decides whether the honey caramelizes or steams. Season with sea salt, cracked black pepper, and red chili flakes, drizzle generously with hot honey, and lay a thin lemon slice on top of each fillet.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_salad": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/kayla-dunham-cucumber-tomato-salad.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 10",
            "heading": "Dress the cucumber and tomatoes",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Slice a Persian cucumber into coins and halve a cup of cherry tomatoes. Toss with a drizzle of extra virgin olive oil, sea salt, and freshly cracked black pepper. Let it sit while the salmon cooks &mdash; the salt pulls juice out of the tomatoes and it becomes its own dressing.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "step_finish": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/kayla-dunham-hot-honey-king-salmon-plated.jpg",
            "subheading": "Minute 15",
            "heading": "Air fry the salmon, then build",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Air fry at 400&deg;F for 8&ndash;10 minutes, until the top is caramelized and the fish flakes at the thin end. Lay a bed of spinach in each bowl, add the cucumber, tomatoes, and sweet potato rounds, and set the salmon on top. Finish with a hard squeeze of lemon.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "step_potato",
        "step_salmon",
        "step_salad",
        "step_finish"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.timeline.presets.name",
