    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_standard": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Leave it better than you found it",
            "heading_size": "title-sm",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "text_standard": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Kayla&rsquo;s motto is the reason this collaboration made sense. Every Seatopia portion ships with a Certificate of Analysis, and the King Salmon in this bowl is third-party lab tested: mercury at <strong>0.017 ppm</strong> &mdash; well under the 0.1 ppm ceiling of the Seatopia Standard &mdash; and <strong>no detectable microplastics</strong> across all six polymers screened.</p><p>One 8.5 oz portion carries <strong>3,434 mg of marine-derived omega-3s</strong> &mdash; 1,142 mg EPA and 2,292 mg DHA, about 172% of a daily omega-3 target &mdash; plus <strong>47 g of protein</strong>, 49 mcg of vitamin D, and around 64 mcg of selenium. Those numbers are printed on the pack itself; you can watch Kayla read them off the label in the video above. Ora King is raised in the cold open water of New Zealand&rsquo;s Marlborough Sounds, and you can read exactly how we test it on our <a href=\"/pages/seatopia-testing-commitment\" title=\"Seatopia's Testing Commitment\">testing commitment page</a>.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
